The difference /24 and /25 
/24 has 256 total ip address with 254 usable address while /25 have 128 total ip address with 126 usable address 
---
Their respective subnet mask is: 
/24 = 255.255.255.0
/25 = 255.255.255.128
---
The two /25 range = 0 - 127 & 0 - 255
---
The calculation for 192.168.1.150/25
32 network bit - /25 network bit = 7 host bits 
block size = 2^7 2*2*2*2*2*2*2 = 128 total ip address 
usuable address = 128 total address - 2(1for network & 1 for broadcast) = 126 usuable address.
first subnet 0 - 127
second subnet 128 - 255
192.168.1.150 falls under second subnet which makes it network address 192.168.1.128
first usuable addr. = 192.168.1.129
last usuable addr. = 192.168.1.254
broadcast addr. = 192.168.1.255
